  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "r1-f1-resolved",
      "class": "follow-up",
      "origin": "pre-existing",
      "at": "payload/.joycraft/runtime/delivery.mjs:118",
      "summary": "Round-1 blocking f1-non-shell-c-accepted is resolved: the -c form needs argv length 3 and a shell basename; /bin/echo -c and node -e 0 -c are refused, with a test. Round-1 f2 (forged footer limit), f3 (readFooter reuse), f4 (receipt outside project) and f5 (shell flag forms in usage text) are also addressed in f4e1df8."
    },
    {
      "id": "f6-exact-words-shell-operator",
      "class": "blocking",
      "origin": "new",
      "criterion": "spec-7-1",
      "at": "payload/.joycraft/runtime/delivery.mjs:117",
      "summary": "When tests.gate holds a shell operator (&&, ||, ;, |; Joycraft's own gate is \"pnpm test && pnpm typecheck\"), the exact-words branch accepts a genuine receipt whose argv is the gate split on spaces. evidence.mjs runs without a shell, so only the first command runs and the rest are its arguments. Probe E1: gate2 is red, the receipt is green, the push lands on the remote. A coordinator that splits the gate on whitespace to call evidence.mjs makes this receipt by itself. Fix: when the gate contains a shell operator, accept only the shell form (sh/bash/... -c \"<gate>\"), and add a test for an && gate run as split words."
    },
    {
      "id": "f7-project-script-named-shell",
      "class": "follow-up",
      "origin": "new",
      "at": "payload/.joycraft/runtime/delivery.mjs:112",
      "summary": "isShell checks only the basename, so a committed no-op script at ./sh or tools/bash passes as a shell while the real gate is red (probe A4, A5). This needs a deliberate fake, the same class as the stated forged-footer limit.",
      "assumption": "The usage text already says a deliberate forgery is not stopped; requiring an absolute or PATH-resolved shell is optional."
    },
    {
      "id": "f8-powershell-flag-case",
      "class": "follow-up",
      "origin": "new",
      "at": "payload/.joycraft/runtime/delivery.mjs:118",
      "summary": "PowerShell takes -command in any case, but only -Command is accepted (probe B3); cmd -c is accepted though cmd uses /c (B4). Both are harmless: the first is a safe refusal, the second cannot run on cmd."
    }
  ],
  "limits": [
    "cmd.exe and powershell are not on this Mac: those forms were checked with hand-written footers only; /usr/bin/BASH does not resolve here, so it was checked by hand footer and /bin/Sh genuinely.",
    "Installed .joycraft/runtime/delivery.mjs is not the reviewed copy; the payload copy was reviewed and run.",
    "Other reviewers had uncommitted files in the tree during the runs."
